From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:48:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 472/488] b12x preparation: no temporary KV cache for a model
 that declares no unit

The state stage built a temporary KV cache and tore it down whenever b12x
was installed on SM12x, whether or not any layer had a plan to tune. A
worker now records when a stage collects a unit of either stage, and only
then builds the temporary cache. With no unit, the weights, profile,
state and bind passes find nothing to prepare and open no session.
---
 tests/model_executor/test_b12x_warmup.py   | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 vllm/model_executor/warmup/b12x_prepare.py |  8 +++++
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py               |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 45 insertions(+)

